  - procedural content generation via machine learning
  - digital games
  - serious games

abstract: >
  Procyon is a modular software architecture for adaptive game level
  generation. It separates integration, orchestration, adaptation,
  persistence, generation, and domain-specific concerns, enabling
  heterogeneous generation algorithms and adaptive dimensions to be
  combined through reusable generation pipelines. The reference
  implementation includes case studies for Fifteen Puzzle, Sudoku,
  and Sokoban, as well as mechanisms for player telemetry, player
  modeling, and adaptive difficulty adjustment.
